	abstract = {This paper demonstrates that sparse autoencoders can scale to extract monosemantic, interpretable features from Claude 3 Sonnet, a state-of-the-art language model. The authors recover features representing abstract, multilingual, and multimodal concepts, including safety-relevant ones like deception and code vulnerabilities. They apply scaling laws to guide training, show that features are behaviorally causal, and provide evidence of structure in feature space.},
